# A continuation line inside an unclosed `(` is not a new statement; the error points at the end (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | where f(a,
b
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..17
  PIPELINE@0..16
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..16
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      CALL_EXPR@10..16
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "f"
        ARG_LIST@11..16
          L_PAREN@11..12 "("
          NAME_REF@12..13
            IDENT@12..13 "a"
          COMMA@13..14 ","
          WHITESPACE@14..15 "\n"
          NAME_REF@15..16
            IDENT@15..16 "b"
  WHITESPACE@16..17 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:1:12
  |
1 | T | where f(a,
  |            ^ this `(` is never closed
2 | b
  |  - the input ends before a `)`
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
